  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">St&#xf6;d till f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttring av r&#xe4;ttshj&#xe4;lps praxis f&#xf6;r ti</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to the Improvement of Legal Aid Practices</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving access to justice in Turkey for disadvantaged groups through the elimination of gaps and needs for an effective functioning legal aid system.
-Improved Automation System for Appointment of Code of Criminal Procedure (CCP)
-Attorneys Enhanced Capacity of the Attorneys Practicing Legal Aid for Disadvantaged Groups
-Improved Performance Evaluation System for Legal Aid Services
-Enhanced Coordination and Cooperation Among the Attorneys Practicing Legal Aid
-Legal aid needs underpinned, and services improved in southern border province of Turkey such as Gaziantep, Hatay, Kilis, Sanliurfa and Kahramanmaras</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The United Nations Development Programme (UNDP) has applied to Sida for funding of 14.5 million SEK to carry out the Project entitled &quot;Support to the Improvement of Legal Aid Practices for Access to Justice for All in Turkey&quot; during the period 2015-2018. 

The intervention aims at an effectively functioning legal aid system that facilitates access to justice in Turkey by 1)improving the Automation System for Appointment of Code of Criminal Procedure (CCP) Attorneys; 2) enhancing the capacity of attorneys practicing legal aid for disadvantaged groups; 3) creating a performance evaluation system for legal aid services; 4) enhancing coordination and cooperation among attorneys for legal aid; 5) and identifying the need for legal aid and improving services in the southern border provinces of Turkey. The UNDP will implement the programme while the Union of Bar Associations of Turkey and the Ministry of Justice will be co-beneficiaries.

The intervention&#x2019;s total budget is 16 million SEK, out of which Sida&apos;s own funding is approximately 14.5 million SEK and the remaining 1.5 million SEK is contributed by the Union of Bar Associations of Turkey.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">UNDP har ans&#xf6;kt om finansiering fr&#xe5;n Sida om SEK 14 500 000 f&#xf6;r att genomf&#xf6;ra projektet &quot;St&#xf6;d till f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttring av r&#xe4;ttshj&#xe4;lpspraxis f&#xf6;r tillg&#xe5;ng till r&#xe4;ttslig pr&#xf6;vning i Turkiet&quot; under perioden 2015-2018.

Insatsen syftar till att bidra till ett effektivt fungerande r&#xe4;ttshj&#xe4;lpssystem som underl&#xe4;ttar tillg&#xe5;ngen till r&#xe4;ttslig pr&#xf6;vning i Turkiet genom 
1) att f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttra systemet genom vilket f&#xf6;rsvarsadvokater utses; 
2) st&#xe4;rka kapaciteten hos advokater som ut&#xf6;var r&#xe4;ttshj&#xe4;lp f&#xf6;r utsatta grupper; 
3) skapa ett system f&#xf6;r resultatutv&#xe4;rdering av r&#xe4;ttshj&#xe4;lp; 
4) st&#xe4;rka samordning och samarbete mellan advokater som sysslar med r&#xe4;ttshj&#xe4;lp; 
5) identifiera behovet av r&#xe4;ttshj&#xe4;lp och f&#xf6;rb&#xe4;ttra servicen i de s&#xf6;dra gr&#xe4;nsprovinserna i Turkiet (d&#xe4;r det finns m&#xe5;nga flyktingar och andra utsatta/svaga grupper). 

UNDP &#xe4;r, tillsammans med det turkiska advokatsamfundet, genomf&#xf6;rare av insatsen.  
Insatsens totala budget uppg&#xe5;r till c:a 16 miljoner kronor, varav Sidas finansiering uppg&#xe5;r till max. SEK 14 500 000 och resterande SEK 1 500 000 kommer fr&#xe5;n det turkiska advokatsamfundet.</narrative>
  </description>
